      "writtenOn": "2026-08-28T07:15:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Apologizes for the confusing statements.\nAfter removing the `PLDM.Entity` interfaces, every D-Bus object created for PLDM entity is no longer needed the `containing`/`contained_by` interfaces anymore.\n\nIn this case, `bmcweb` can retrieves the state for the D-Bus object using the general approach. \n\nFor example, for a terminus contains Cpu under itself and it may consists of state sensor monitoring for the state set `Health`. \n\n`pldmd` should creates a D-Bus object with appropriate interface (`xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.Cpu`), representing it is a Cpu. In addition, the D-Bus object should also be having interface `xyz.openbmc_project.State.Decorator.OperationalStatus` for the health property it is holding. \n\nWhenever a redfish request arrives, `bmcweb` can retrieves the D-Bus object path, using the ID and object type parsed from the request.\nAfter that, required properties can be retrieves by through hardcoded interface name in each `bmcweb` function.",
